{"name":"Borneo","hex":"#a76244","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Borneo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A Pacific island shared by Brunei, Indonesia, and Malaysia; the world’s third largest island."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Borneo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Borneo","blocks":[{"text":"Borneo is the third-largest island in the world, with an area of 748,168 km2 (288,869 sq mi), and population of 23,053,723. Situated at the geographic centre of Maritime Southeast Asia, it is one of the Greater Sunda Islands, located north of Java, west of Sulawesi, and east of Sumatra. The island is crossed by the equator, which divides it roughly in half. In Indonesia, the island is also known as Kalimantan, which is also the name of the Indonesian region located on the island. The rest of the island consists of East Malaysia and Brunei."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Administrative_map_of_Borneo_%28Indonesian%29.png/330px-Administrative_map_of_Borneo_%28Indonesian%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borneo","wikidata":"Q36117"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Borneo_Topography.png/500px-Borneo_Topography.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Borneo_Topography.png/1280px-Borneo_Topography.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Borneo_Topography.png/500px-Borneo_Topography.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABorneo_Topography.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Jack_fish_and_reef_sharks.jpg/500px-Jack_fish_and_reef_sharks.jpg?utm_sourc